# RedeemTrip Project Rules

- Read `AGENTS.md` before making changes.
- Read `docs/prd.md`, `docs/trd.md`, and `docs/tasks.md` when implementing product features.
- Use TypeScript and follow the existing project conventions.
- Use the existing Next.js App Router structure.
- Do not introduce unrelated refactoring.
- Validate external input with Zod.
- Keep secrets server-side.
- Enforce authentication and resource ownership.
- Do not invent provider API capabilities, prices, availability, or credentials.
- Use deterministic code for financial calculations and recommendation ranking.
- AI output must be validated before use.
- Update `docs/tasks.md` when completing implementation tasks.
- Run relevant linting, type checking, and tests.
- If requirements are unclear, identify the ambiguity before making a significant architectural decision.
